    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>The CP12 gets all the attention. It is not the whole job. Gas firms also write boiler service records, commissioning forms and breakdown reports every week. Most of it is written by hand, in the van, after the boiler is cold. Gas engineer field reporting software records it while you are still at the appliance.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Six jobs a day means six sets of paperwork. On paper, that is done from memory in the van.</li><li>Service records, commissioning forms and breakdown reports need different content. They share one problem.</li><li>Landlords and agents want digital records the same day.</li><li>A voice note on the job beats typing from memory later. It keeps the time.</li><li>One WhatsApp way covers CP12s, commissioning forms and breakdown reports.</li><li>The Gas Safety (Installation and Use) Regulations 1998 still need a written record with set fields.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The real scope",
      "heading": "More than the CP12",
      "html": "<p>The CP12 is the landlord gas safety record. The law sets its fields. It is one of several records.</p><p>A <strong>boiler service</strong> gives a service record. Work done, readings, condition of parts. It goes to the owner or agent and backs up the warranty.</p><p>A <strong>commissioning visit</strong> gives a commissioning form. Gas rate, pressure, flue readings, and your sign-off.</p><p>A <strong>breakdown visit</strong> gives a report. Fault, parts, work done, outcome. It is also the basis of the invoice.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The root problem",
      "heading": "In the van afterwards",
      "html": "<p>Writing up in the van is normal. It is also the problem.</p><p>Recall fades. A flue CO of 42ppm at 11:15 is written up at 12:30. Most times it is right. Sometimes it is close. Sometimes it is wrong.</p><p>Six jobs means six forms. The last one of the day is the worst. Short entries like \"Boiler serviced, satisfactory\" prove nothing.</p>"
    },
