      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What paperwork do gas engineers complete on site?</h3><p>CP12 certificates, boiler service records, commissioning forms, breakdown reports, gas tightness tests, and purging and pressure tests. Each has its own content.</p><h3>Must boiler service records be kept?</h3><p>There is no set time, as there is for CP12s. Records still back up warranty claims and help in a dispute. Most firms keep them at least 2 to 3 years.</p><h3>What should a gas breakdown report include?</h3><p>Date, time, address, customer or landlord, appliance make, model and age, the fault, work done, parts with numbers, the outcome, any more work needed, your name and Gas Safe number.</p><h3>Can voice notes be gas site records?</h3><p>A voice recording alone is not enough. The 1998 Regulations need a written record with set fields. A voice note works if it is written out into those fields. Quickler does that.</p>"
